[2.235342, "o", "Report?     yes\r\r\nSummary     An insufficient session expiration vulnerability in the ArubaOS command line interface allows an attacker to keep a session running on an affected device after the removal of the impacted account.\r\r\nProduct     ArubaOS command line interface\r\r\nCWE         unknown\r\r\nCVSS 3.1    CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H  ->  8.8 High\r\r\nNo evidence AC, PR, UI, S\r\r\nConfidence  low\r\r\nFlags       -\r\r\nNext step   Obtain full technical details: vendor advisory or proof-of-concept demonstrating session persistence after account removal, and affected ArubaOS versions.\r\r\nEvidence\r\r\n  - Vulnerability description: \"An insufficient session expiration vulnerability exists in the ArubaOS command line interface.\"\r\r\n  - Impact — attacker can keep session after account removal: \"Successful exploitation of this vulnerability allows an attacker to keep a session running on an affected device after the removal of the impacted account\"\r\r\n\r\r\n[a]pprove  [e]dit  [r]eject > "]
